## 1. Purpose

This Service Level Agreement ("SLA") defines the service levels {{ f.company.name }} ("HPL") commits to for its warehousing and transportation customers, how performance is measured, and the service credits available when HPL misses a target. It forms part of each customer's master services agreement.

## 2. Definitions

- **Promised date** - the delivery date communicated to the customer when the shipment is booked: ship date plus the standard transit time for the destination zone.
- **On-time delivery** - a shipment delivered on or before its promised date.
- **On-time delivery rate** - on-time shipments divided by all delivered shipments in the measurement period, excluding the shipments listed in Section 5.
- **Order accuracy** - orders shipped with the correct items and quantities, divided by all orders shipped.
- **Dock-to-stock time** - time from inbound check-in until goods are available for picking.
- **Measurement period** - one {{ f.sla.measurement }}.

## 3. Service Levels

| Metric | Target |
|---|---|
| On-time delivery rate | at least {{ f.sla.on_time_target_pct }}% |
| Order accuracy | at least {{ f.sla.order_accuracy_target_pct }}% |
| Dock-to-stock time | within {{ f.sla.dock_to_stock_hours }} hours |
| Inquiry first response | by customer tier (Section 6) |

## 4. Service Credits

4.1 If HPL's on-time delivery rate for a customer falls below target in a measurement period, the customer is entitled to a service credit calculated on that period's total freight charges for the customer:

| On-time delivery rate in the period | Service credit |
|---|---|
| {{ f.sla.credit_tier_2.below_pct }}% up to (but not including) {{ f.sla.credit_tier_1.below_pct }}% | {{ f.sla.credit_tier_1.credit_pct }}% of the period's freight charges |
| below {{ f.sla.credit_tier_2.below_pct }}% | {{ f.sla.credit_tier_2.credit_pct }}% of the period's freight charges |

4.2 Credits do not stack: the single applicable tier is applied. The maximum credit in any period is {{ f.sla.credit_tier_2.credit_pct }}% of freight charges.

4.3 Customers must request a credit in writing within 60 days after the end of the measurement period. Credits are applied to the next invoice and are the customer's sole remedy for missed service levels.

## 5. Exclusions

The following shipments are excluded from the on-time delivery calculation:

5.1 **Force majeure.** Shipments delayed by events outside HPL's and its carriers' reasonable control - including severe weather, road closures, natural disasters and government actions - provided the event is documented on the shipment record (for example as a weather hold noting the affected route).

5.2 **Customer-caused delays.** Late order release (after the same-day cut-off of {{ f.dock_rules.same_day_cutoff }}), incorrect or incomplete delivery addresses, consignee not available, or delivery appointments requested by the customer for a date later than the promised date.

5.3 **Shipments not yet delivered** at the end of the period are measured in the period in which they are delivered.

